  "headline": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka Formally Resigns As Indonesian Vice President",
  "seoTitle": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka Resigns as Indonesian Vice President",
  "metaDescription": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka has formally resigned as Vice President of Indonesia, prompting constitutional consultations led by President Prabowo Subianto.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Gibran Rakabuming Raka submitted a formal five-paragraph resignation letter directly to President Prabowo Subianto at the State Palace.",
    "Official statements confirm the letter does not specify a reason for the resignation, with officials describing the matter as personal.",
    "The government is currently engaged in constitutional consultations with the People's Consultative Assembly to manage the vacancy."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Gibran Rakabuming Raka officially resigned from his position as the Vice President of Indonesia. The resignation was formalized through the submission of a document to President Prabowo Subianto at the State Palace. Following the event, Coordinating Minister for Law, Human Rights, Immigration, and Correctional Affairs, Yusril Ihza Mahendra, noted that the resignation does not require approval from the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR). However, President Prabowo has initiated discussions with cabinet ministers and MPR leadership to ensure the constitutional processes for handling the vacancy are followed correctly. Reports indicate that the MPR has a 60-day window to address the appointment of a definitive vice president. While the former vice president's letter cited personal reasons, it remained brief and did not detail specific motivations for the departure, according to government officials and parliamentary leadership.",
